+ * answer here had none. bluetoothd's vendor-command parsers (bcm_vsc.c, aci_vsc.c: 43 of them) only assert that at
+ * least N bytes are left, never an exact length, and the most any reads is _BCM_LowPowerCoreStatsEventParser's ~212
+ * bytes; so every vendor command is now answered with 240 bytes of zeros after the status (BD_VSC_FACTORY_CAL_
+ * READ_TABLE's first still 0x51). Also: a Command Status' status was read from its length byte in 0975's status
